E. what did the enumeration assume about the revealed capitols?
==============================================================================
  revealed capitols (published 0): [(5, 7), (10, 5)]
    (5, 7): inside a drawn state? NO - its state size was left FREE
    (10, 5): inside a drawn state? NO - its state size was left FREE
  in check_partial the revealed 0-cells are added to `known_capitals` but
  NOT to `known_size`, so their state size is never fixed to 1.
  the singleton that WAS forced is (5,10), from d(4,10)=1:
     cost((4,10)->(5,10)) = min(|S(4,10)|, |S(5,10)|) = 1
     and |S(4,10)| = 1 is impossible (a singleton reads 0, not 1)
     => |S(5,10)| = 1.  Sound.
